| AOG events / yr | {{RESULT:policies.P0.aog_events}} {{RESULT:policies.P0.aog_events_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P1.aog_events}} {{RESULT:policies.P1.aog_events_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P2.aog_events}} {{RESULT:policies.P2.aog_events_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.I125.aog_events}} {{RESULT:policies.I125.aog_events_ci}} |
| Spares capital | {{RESULT:policies.P0.spare_capital_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.P0.spare_capital_aed_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P1.spare_capital_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.P1.spare_capital_aed_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P2.spare_capital_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.P2.spare_capital_aed_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.I125.spare_capital_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.I125.spare_capital_aed_ci}} |
| Annual operating cost excl. AOG penalty | {{RESULT:policies.P0.opex_ex_penalty_aed}} | {{RESULT:policies.P1.opex_ex_penalty_aed}} | {{RESULT:policies.P2.opex_ex_penalty_aed}} | {{RESULT:policies.I125.opex_ex_penalty_aed}} |
| Annual AOG penalty, scenario | {{RESULT:policies.P0.aog_penalty_aed}} | {{RESULT:policies.P1.aog_penalty_aed}} | {{RESULT:policies.P2.aog_penalty_aed}} | {{RESULT:policies.I125.aog_penalty_aed}} |
| Total annual cost (opex + penalty) | {{RESULT:policies.P0.total_annual_cost_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.P0.total_annual_cost_aed_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P1.total_annual_cost_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.P1.total_annual_cost_aed_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P2.total_annual_cost_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.P2.total_annual_cost_aed_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.I125.total_annual_cost_aed}} {{RESULT:policies.I125.total_annual_cost_aed_ci}} |
| Paired difference in AOG hours vs P0 | — | {{RESULT:policies.P1_vs_P0.delta_aog_hours}} {{RESULT:policies.P1_vs_P0.delta_aog_hours_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P2_vs_P0.delta_aog_hours}} {{RESULT:policies.P2_vs_P0.delta_aog_hours_ci}} | n/a ¹ |
| Paired difference in AOG hours vs P2 | {{RESULT:policies.P0_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours}} {{RESULT:policies.P0_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours_ci}} | {{RESULT:policies.P1_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours}} {{RESULT:policies.P1_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours_ci}} | — | {{RESULT:frontier.recommended_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours}} {{RESULT:frontier.recommended_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours_ci}} |

¹ The frontier holdout run recorded paired differences against the base policy P2 only, so no paired I125 − P0 interval exists. Money is AED; CIs on money are in AED millions.

**Selection versus holdout.** The recommended point was chosen on selection seeds 100–119, where it scored {{RESULT:frontier.recommended.selection_aog_hours}} of material AOG a year {{RESULT:frontier.recommended.selection_aog_hours_ci}}. On the holdout it scored {{RESULT:frontier.recommended.aog_hours}} ({{RESULT:frontier.recommended.selection_shift_pct}}), and the selection value lies outside the holdout CI. P2 moved the same way but less ({{RESULT:policies.P2.selection_aog_hours}} on selection, {{RESULT:policies.P2.aog_hours}} on holdout, {{RESULT:policies.P2.selection_shift_pct}}): the plan picked on selection seeds lost the most, a winner's-curse effect. The paired gap to P2 held ({{RESULT:frontier.recommended_vs_P2.selection_delta}} on selection, {{RESULT:frontier.recommended_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours}} {{RESULT:frontier.recommended_vs_P2.delta_aog_hours_ci}} on holdout), and the ranking P0 > P1 > P2 > I125 on AOG hours held.

**Where the methods do not win.** {{RESULT:readme.not_win_summary}}

These are results on simulated data from assumed parameters. They show that the method works and how large the effects can be under those assumptions. They are not a forecast of any real airline's performance.

